From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Subject: [PATCH] Migrate 0382-oom-fix-03-transcode-waits-for-memory.patch

Source: 0382-oom-fix-03-transcode-waits-for-memory.patch
Moved by hand: applies unchanged once 0181 (bad-alloc fallbacks) is in

Core patch, for tools/eglantine-patches after oom-fix-02, whose vk_texture_cache.h it builds on.
Paths are the submodule's.

Zelda on next16, crash-20261106-023800, ended on GPUBack: UploadImageContents, TranscodeAstcToBcn,
StagingBufferPool::Request, CreateStagingBuffer, CreateBuffer, terminate. The request is the BC3
output of a 3072x3072 12-level ASTC image: EDEN_STAGING_OOM asked=12582960 made=16777216 usage=0,
and 3072^2 x 4/3 + 48 is that size.

Why nothing caught it:
- Request throws by design; only TryRequest catches, and the transcode called Request.
- The retry in CreateStagingBuffer asks for the same 16 MiB: the smaller size is only for buffers
  the CPU maps, because Holds() cannot tell the size of the others. Its second refusal is outside
  the try.
- 0181's catch in RefreshContents is for std::bad_alloc.
- The reserve lent nothing because it was under its floor: EDEN_RESERVE_LENT 0 MiB, 120 to 125 blocks
  left, floor 128 (256 MiB). Lending stops there by design.

And the transcode was already lost: just before, the decode image (3072x3072, 12 levels, format 51,
VkFormat A8B8G8R8) "does not fit; using an unbacked sparse image". The decode ran into an image with
nothing bound. On the console an unbound range is mapped read-write to the driver's one zero block,
so that decode lands in the block every unbound range reads as zero. Likely, from the source of
radv_ps5_vrange_unbind; not seen on a console.

Now, using what the code has (TryRequest, UploadLater):
- No decode image at all (CreateImage threw, which ended the session): no decode.
- No output buffer: the decode is recorded, so its image goes to pending_transcodes with the tick.
  The local used to die in the unwinding, with the GPU still to use it.
With EDEN_NX2_TRANSCODE_WAIT=1 also:
- A decode image with nothing bound: no decode.
- During the 250 ms pause after a refusal, no decode is begun.
In all of these the runtime says so (TakeUploadRefused) and RefreshContents calls UploadLater: the
image is uploaded at its next use. It shows nothing until then, and a small cost is paid per use.

The aborts need no switch. Changed for next18: the two cases under the switch were no abort, so
they are asked for. The source had them on, with EDEN_NX2_TRANSCODE_UNBACKED=1 to go back; that name
is gone, and unset now means the same thing it did. The reserve's floor already has a switch:
EDEN_GUEST_RESERVE_FLOOR=64 lends 128 MiB.

Not covered: the DeviceLocal Requests in vk_compute_pass.cpp (lines 349, 400, 458) throw the same way.

Proven: as oom-fix-02, same harness and results; the anchor on `pending_transcodes.push_back` still
matches once, which is why the refused path says emplace_back. 02 and 03 apply before or after
mem-audit 01, 02 and 04, on core16. Not linked, not run. Likely: a 12 MiB buffer fits on a later try.
The pool stayed at 0 to 6 MiB free through this run's last refusals, so this may only move the end.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_staging_buffer_pool.h b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_staging_buffer_pool.h
index 011a06f7ab..5ee05a5670 100644
--- a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_staging_buffer_pool.h
+++ b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_staging_buffer_pool.h
@@ -48,6 +48,10 @@ public:
     /// waits for the GPU.
     std::optional<StagingBufferRef> TryRequest(size_t size, MemoryUsage usage,
                                                bool deferred = false);
+    /// Whether the pause after a refusal (TryRequest) is on: work that needs a new buffer can wait.
+    [[nodiscard]] bool RefusedJustNow() const noexcept {
+        return std::chrono::steady_clock::now() < refused_until;
+    }
     /// A small download buffer made at the start and kept, for when no other can be had. One user
     /// at a time: the GPU thread, which waits for its copies before it uses the buffer again.
     [[nodiscard]] StagingBufferRef ReservedDownload() noexcept;
diff --git a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_texture_cache.cpp b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_texture_cache.cpp
index 3f5ed42cc5..00ccabdcbe 100644
--- a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_texture_cache.cpp
+++ b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_texture_cache.cpp
@@ -4887,6 +4887,18 @@ void TextureCacheRuntime::TranscodeAstcToBcn(
     const u32 levels = static_cast<u32>(info.resources.levels);
     const u32 layers = static_cast<u32>(info.resources.layers);
     constexpr VkFormat DecodeFormat = VK_FORMAT_A8B8G8R8_UNORM_PACK32;
+    // EDEN_NX2_TRANSCODE_WAIT=1: with memory refused the upload waits for the image's next use
+    // rather than begin a decode that is lost. A decode into an image with nothing bound lands, on
+    // the console, in the block every unbound range reads as zero. Unset, it decodes as before.
+    static const bool wait_for_memory = [] {
+        const char* const value = std::getenv("EDEN_NX2_TRANSCODE_WAIT");
+        return value != nullptr && value[0] == '1';
+    }();
+    // The pool refused something a moment ago: this would decode, and be refused its output.
+    if (wait_for_memory && staging_buffer_pool.RefusedJustNow()) {
+        upload_refused = true;
+        return;
+    }
     // A decode image of the same shape the GPU is done with: title 1's title screen decodes
     // dozens of textures a frame, mostly of a few shapes. Making one took 263 us; from VMA's
     // shared blocks 90 us, but freeing them there left ~1 GB of those blocks unused.
@@ -4898,9 +4910,11 @@ void TextureCacheRuntime::TranscodeAstcToBcn(
         pending = std::move(*reusable);
         free_transcodes.erase(reusable);
     } else {
-        pending = PendingTranscode{
-            .tick = 0,
-            .image = memory_allocator.CreateImage(VkImageCreateInfo{
+        // With no memory the allocator gives an image with nothing bound (or, with no room for
+        // that either, throws).
+        vk::Image decode_image;
+        try {
+            decode_image = memory_allocator.CreateImage(VkImageCreateInfo{
                 .sType = VK_STRUCTURE_TYPE_IMAGE_CREATE_INFO,
                 .pNext = nullptr,
                 .flags = 0,
@@ -4916,7 +4930,19 @@ void TextureCacheRuntime::TranscodeAstcToBcn(
                 .queueFamilyIndexCount = 0,
                 .pQueueFamilyIndices = nullptr,
                 .initialLayout = VK_IMAGE_LAYOUT_UNDEFINED,
-            }, true),
+            }, true);
+        } catch (const vk::Exception& refused) {
+            if (refused.GetResult() != VK_ERROR_OUT_OF_DEVICE_MEMORY) {
+                throw;
+            }
+        }
+        if (!decode_image || (wait_for_memory && decode_image.IsUnbacked())) {
+            upload_refused = true;
+            return;
+        }
+        pending = PendingTranscode{
+            .tick = 0,
+            .image = std::move(decode_image),
             .views = {},
             .width = width,
             .height = height,
@@ -4967,11 +4993,20 @@ void TextureCacheRuntime::TranscodeAstcToBcn(
         });
         total += size;
     }
-    const auto output = staging_buffer_pool.Request(total, MemoryUsage::DeviceLocal);
+    // Zelda ended here on 2026-11-06: Request throws when refused, a buffer only the GPU uses has
+    // no smaller size to try, and nothing on the GPU thread catches it. Now the upload is done at the
+    // image's next use instead. The decode is recorded: its image stays until the GPU is past it.
+    const auto output = staging_buffer_pool.TryRequest(total, MemoryUsage::DeviceLocal);
+    if (!output) {
+        pending.tick = scheduler.CurrentTick();
+        pending_transcodes.emplace_back(std::move(pending));
+        upload_refused = true;
+        return;
+    }
     for (u32 level = 0; level < levels; ++level) {
         bc_encoder_pass->Encode(*pending.views[level], copies[level].image_extent.width,
-                                copies[level].image_extent.height, layers, bc3, output.buffer,
-                                output.offset, total, copies[level].buffer_offset);
+                                copies[level].image_extent.height, layers, bc3, output->buffer,
+                                output->offset, total, copies[level].buffer_offset);
     }
     scheduler.Record([](vk::CommandBuffer cmdbuf) {
         const VkMemoryBarrier barrier{
@@ -4983,7 +5018,7 @@ void TextureCacheRuntime::TranscodeAstcToBcn(
         cmdbuf.PipelineBarrier(VK_PIPELINE_STAGE_COMPUTE_SHADER_BIT, VK_PIPELINE_STAGE_TRANSFER_BIT,
                                0, barrier);
     });
-    image.UploadMemory(output.buffer, output.offset, copies);
+    image.UploadMemory(output->buffer, output->offset, copies);
     pending.tick = scheduler.CurrentTick();
     pending_transcodes.push_back(std::move(pending));
 }
diff --git a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_texture_cache.h b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_texture_cache.h
index 9a4e29f7a9..f73924c5e5 100644
--- a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_texture_cache.h
+++ b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_texture_cache.h
@@ -11,6 +11,7 @@
 #include <memory>
 #include <optional>
 #include <span>
+#include <utility>
 
 #include "video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache_base.h"
 
@@ -67,6 +68,12 @@ public:
 
     std::optional<StagingBufferRef> TryUploadStagingBuffer(size_t size, bool deferred = false);
 
+    /// Whether the last AccelerateImageUpload put nothing in the image for want of memory, and
+    /// the upload is still to do. Asking clears it.
+    [[nodiscard]] bool TakeUploadRefused() noexcept {
+        return std::exchange(upload_refused, false);
+    }
+
     /// Runs `make`, which makes an image, and says if it did: false when the device refused it
     /// memory and an image with nothing bound too. On the console the exception reaches here
     /// through the image's slot (headless/slot_vector_recovery.cmake).
@@ -282,6 +289,9 @@ public:
     void TranscodeAstcToBcn(Image& image, const StagingBufferRef& map,
                             std::span<const VideoCommon::SwizzleParameters> swizzles);
 
+    /// See TakeUploadRefused.
+    bool upload_refused = false;
+
     /// Temporary decode images, reusable once the GPU is past `tick`.
     struct PendingTranscode {
         u64 tick;
diff --git a/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h b/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h
index 2ecf45611c..5ee22b2876 100644
--- a/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h
+++ b/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h
@@ -1937,7 +1937,15 @@ void TextureCache<P>::RefreshContents(Image& image, ImageId image_id) {
         if (!UploadInChunks(image)) {
             if (auto staging = UploadStagingNow(runtime, MapSizeBytes(image))) {
                 UploadImageContents(image, *staging);
-                runtime.InsertUploadMemoryBarrier();
+                bool refused = false;
+                if constexpr (requires { runtime.TakeUploadRefused(); }) {
+                    refused = runtime.TakeUploadRefused();
+                }
+                if (refused) {
+                    UploadLater(image);
+                } else {
+                    runtime.InsertUploadMemoryBarrier();
+                }
             } else if (!UploadInChunks(image, 0)) {
                 UploadLater(image);
             }
